{
  "concept": "Every ellipse is organized around its center by four named parts — vertices, co-vertices, and foci — whose positions are fixed by the semi-major axis a, the semi-minor axis b, and the focal distance c, related by c² = a² − b².",
  "figureType": "diagram",
  "elements": [
    "Horizontal x-axis with arrowheads at both ends, label 'x' at right end",
    "Vertical y-axis with arrowheads at both ends, label 'y' at top",
    "Blue ellipse outline centered at the origin, wider than tall (horizontal major axis)",
    "Red dashed horizontal segment from left vertex to right vertex lying on the x-axis (major axis)",
    "Red dashed vertical segment from bottom co-vertex to top co-vertex lying on the y-axis (minor axis)",
    "Black dot at origin labeled 'Center'",
    "Black dots at (±a, 0) where the ellipse meets the x-axis, each labeled 'Vertex'",
    "Black dots at (0, ±b) where the ellipse meets the y-axis, each labeled 'Co-vertex' (top) and 'Co-vertex' (bottom)",
    "Two small green dots on the major axis at (±c, 0), inside the vertices, each labeled 'Focus'",
    "Text label 'Major Axis' below the left half of the horizontal dashed segment",
    "Text label 'Minor Axis' to the right of the upper half of the vertical dashed segment",
    "Alternate (toggled) parameter labels: brace/arrow marking 'a' from center to right vertex, 'b' from center to top co-vertex, 'c' from center to right focus",
    "Alternate (toggled) readout of the standard equation x²/a² + y²/b² = 1 with live numeric values of a, b, c and the relation c² = a² − b²",
    "Optional draggable point P on the ellipse with two straight segments P→left focus and P→right focus, annotated with their lengths and their sum"
  ],
  "interactions": [
    {
      "id": "semiMajorA",
      "type": "slider",
      "teaches": "a is the distance from the center to a vertex: increasing it stretches the ellipse horizontally, pushing the vertices outward while the center and co-vertices stay put, and dragging the foci farther apart.",
      "label": "Semi-major axis a",
      "range": [1, 8, 0.1],
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "semiMinorB",
      "type": "slider",
      "teaches": "b is the distance from the center to a co-vertex: it controls only the height, moving the co-vertices while the vertices stay fixed — and as b approaches a the foci slide toward the center.",
      "label": "Semi-minor axis b",
      "range": [1, 8, 0.1],
      "default": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "labelMode",
      "type": "toggle",
      "teaches": "Each named anatomical part corresponds to a number in the standard equation: vertex ↔ a, co-vertex ↔ b, focus ↔ c, with c² = a² − b².",
      "label": "Label mode",
      "options": ["Feature names", "Equation parameters"],
      "default": "Feature names"
    },
    {
      "id": "dragPointOnEllipse",
      "type": "drag",
      "teaches": "Why the foci are special: no matter where the point sits on the curve, the sum of its distances to the two foci stays equal to 2a."
    }
  ],
  "demo_steps": [
    {
      "title": "The named parts",
      "narration": "A horizontal ellipse with its center at the origin. The red dashed major axis runs between the two vertices; the red dashed minor axis runs between the two co-vertices; two green foci sit on the major axis inside the vertices.",
      "state": { "semiMajorA": 6, "semiMinorB": 4, "labelMode": "Feature names" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Stretch the major axis",
      "narration": "Increase a and only the width changes: the vertices slide outward, the co-vertices never move, and the foci spread farther apart as the ellipse grows more elongated.",
      "state": { "semiMajorA": 8, "semiMinorB": 4, "labelMode": "Feature names" }
    },
    {
      "title": "Stretch the minor axis",
      "narration": "Now hold a and raise b: the co-vertices rise, the vertices stay anchored, and the foci creep toward the center because c = √(a² − b²) shrinks.",
      "state": { "semiMajorA": 8, "semiMinorB": 7, "labelMode": "Feature names" }
    },
    {
      "title": "When a = b the ellipse is a circle",
      "narration": "Set b equal to a and c becomes zero — both foci collapse onto the center, the axes become equal, and the ellipse is just a circle of radius a.",
      "state": { "semiMajorA": 6, "semiMinorB": 6, "labelMode": "Feature names" }
    },
    {
      "title": "From parts to equation",
      "narration": "Switch to parameter labels: the center-to-vertex distance is a, the center-to-co-vertex distance is b, and the center-to-focus distance is c, feeding directly into x²/a² + y²/b² = 1 with c² = a² − b².",
      "state": { "semiMajorA": 6, "semiMinorB": 4, "labelMode": "Equation parameters" }
    },
    {
      "title": "The focal definition",
      "narration": "Drag the point around the curve and watch the two focal distances trade off — their sum is always 2a, the full length of the major axis.",
      "state": { "semiMajorA": 6, "semiMinorB": 3, "labelMode": "Equation parameters" }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "The ellipse's anatomy is just three distances measured from the center — a to a vertex, b to a co-vertex, c to a focus — locked together by c² = a² − b², so changing the shape moves the foci automatically.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "Centered Cartesian axes drawn thin and black with arrowheads at all four ends, 'x' labeled at the right tip and italic 'y' at the top tip. A single blue (medium-thick, steel-blue) ellipse outline centered on the origin, noticeably wider than tall in the default view. Red dashed straight segments lie exactly on the axes, spanning vertex-to-vertex horizontally and co-vertex-to-co-vertex vertically. Black filled dots mark center, both vertices, and both co-vertices; two smaller bright-green dots mark the foci on the horizontal dashed line, roughly two-thirds of the way out toward the vertices in the default state. Serif text labels: 'Vertex' outside each end of the major axis, 'Co-vertex' above the top dot and below the bottom dot, 'Focus' above each green dot, 'Center' just below-right of the origin dot, 'Major Axis' under the left half of the horizontal segment, 'Minor Axis' to the right of the upper vertical segment. In 'Equation parameters' mode the word labels are replaced by dimension arrows from the center to the right vertex ('a'), center to top co-vertex ('b'), and center to right focus ('c'), plus a small corner panel showing x²/a² + y²/b² = 1 and c² = a² − b² with live numeric values. The draggable point is an orange dot on the curve with two thin gray lines to the green foci and a readout r₁ + r₂ = 2a. Keep the viewport fixed so the learner perceives the ellipse growing and shrinking rather than the axes rescaling."
}

